-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/DALO> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithology> "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/PSAMM"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/HWH> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithology> "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/ASH"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/LBN> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithology> "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SLST"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/MVCA> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithology> "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/GB"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/ALFRD> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Major intrusions of the Scottish Highlands Ordovician Suite (HIO) that occur in the Alford district and consist of dioritic to granitic rock. They are lithologically associated (diorite, quartz-diorite, tonalite, granodiorite and granite), and lithologically distinct from other intrusions of the Scottish Highlands Ordovician Suite."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/BURRA> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Granite."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CLUNY> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Includes Syllavethy Quartz-diorite-granodiorite Pluton (SYLL), Tillyfourie Tonalite Pluton (TLYF), and Syllavethy-Tillyfourie Tonalite-granodiorite Vein-swarm."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/ESHET> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Major intrusions of the Shetland Islands Suite (SHEGR) that occur east of Walls Boundary Fault."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/HIO> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "All components of the Caledonian Supersuite (CIGSS) that occur within the Northern Highlands and Grampian Highlands regions and formed broadly in association with the Grampian Event. This is the older (Ordovician) of the two main tectonothermal events of the Caledonian Orogeny in Scotland."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/HNTL> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Gabbro, peridotite."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/HTKN> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "[Obsolete: use HNTL, KNOC]"@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/KNDL> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Comprises a lower sequence of graded siltstone-mudstone couplets with locally extensive intercalations of turbiditic sandstone (Bannisdale Formation)."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/KNOC> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Gabbro, peridotite."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/LAMM> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Metagabbro with subsidiary metadolerite."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/LBN> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Limestone and siltstone."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/LLT> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Ludfordian."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/LWH> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "[Obsolete]"@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/MSHET> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Minor intrusions of the Shetland Islands Suite (SHEGR) not assigned to other subsuites. Includes the Yell Pegmatitic granite Vein-swarm (YPS) as well as unnamed minor intrusions of granite, felsite, mafite, microtonalite, microdiorite, dolerite, and lamprophyre."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/NEBAS> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Major intrusions of the Scottish Highlands Ordovician Suite (HIO) that occur within the north-east part of the Grampian Highlands region and consist dominantly of basic rock."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/NEGRA> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Major intrusions of the Scottish Highlands Ordovician Suite (HIO) that occur in the north-east part of the Grampian Highlands region and consist of granitic rock. The intrusions have a distinctive lithological association (two mica granite, generally pervasively deformed). \r\n\r\nAll intrusions are emplaced in the Dalradian Supergroup (DALN) (c.f. Northwest Grampian Granitic Subsuite (NWGRA))."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/NMVN> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Includes the Ronas Hill Granite Pluton (ROHG), East Northmaven Granite Sheet (EAST), Mangaster Voe Diorite-gabbro Pluton (MGVO), Roerwater Gabbro-diorite Intrusion (ROER), Hevdadale Gabbro-diorite Intrusion (HVDD), Housetter Granite Intrusion (HOUG), Ronas Voe Intrusion-breccia Intrusion Swarm (RVBR), and Muckle Row Granite Pluton (MURO) as well as other intrusions of granite, gabbro, diorite, granodiorite and ultramafic-rock."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/NWGRA> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Major intrusions of the Scottish Highlands Ordovician Suite (HIO) that occur in the north-west part of the Grampian Highlands region and consist of granitic rock. The intrusions have a clear lithological association (granite with primary muscovite and biotite mica and locally granodiorite, locally pervasively deformed). \r\n\r\nThe intrusions are emplaced mainly in the Dava (DAVA) and Glen Banchor (GLBA) successions (c.f. Northeast Grampian Granitic Subsuite (NEGRA))."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/OBFE> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Sheets and other intrusions of agglomerate, basalt, felsite, analcime-gabbro, olivine-microgabbro and syenitic-rock."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/ODMIV> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "[Obsolete: use OBFE]"@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/OLNA> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Includes the Brae Diorite–ultramafic Pluton (BRAEP) as well as unnamed intrusions of granodiorite, diorite, and ultramafic-rock."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/UWH> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "[Obsolete]"@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/WHGN> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Includes the Cairn Trench Granite Pluton (CTGR) and Ben Tirran Granitic Intrusion-swarm."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/WHIP> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "[Obsolete: use BURRA, WHITH] Aplitic microgranite, diorite and pegmatitic granite."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/WHITH> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Diorite."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/WHITL> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Includes the South Burn of Burrafirth Granitic Pluton (BURRA) and the Whitelaw Hill Diorite Intrusion (WHITH) as well as several unnamed intrusions of ultramafic-rock."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/WSHET> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Major intrusions of the Shetland Islands Suite (SHEGR) that occur west of Walls Boundary Fault."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/KNDL> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLowerBoundaryDefinition> "As for the base of the Bannisdale Formation; gradational from the sandstone-dominated Coniston Group into siltstone and mudstone units."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/HNTL> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasObsoleteEquivalent> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/HTKN> .
